title: Women's Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: psoe_in_government = 1 and womens_rights_timer = 0
on-arrival: womens_rights_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/es/leaders/de_la_torre.jpg
frequency: 50
max-visits: 6

= Women's Rights

The 1931 Constitution grants women the vote and formal equality before the law - won against real resistance even within our own party, where Indalecio Prieto and others feared women would vote for the clergy's candidates rather than the Republic's. But that formal equality is far from realized in practice. Women in the workforce are not paid equally for the same work, and are often pushed out of employment after marriage. Family and property law still heavily favor men. And that is not to mention the overwhelming weight of Catholic social custom.

For better or worse, the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> stand virtually alone in pressing for further reform on women's status, and even within the party, the leadership does not consider it a priority. [? if psoe_r < 25 : Unfortunately, women still disproportionately support the clerical parties. ?]

- @labor: Institute policies that help women in the workforce.
- @family: Reform marriage, divorce, and property law.
- @welfare: Improve welfare for single mothers and children.
- @liberalize: Attempt to liberalize the law on family planning.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@labor
subtitle: Paid maternity leave, equal-pay provisions, and so on.
on-arrival: womens_work += 1; womens_rights += 1; industrial_psoe -= 4 if unemployed > 15; urban_middle_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 0.1;
max-visits: 3

These policies mean our party is growing in popularity among working women. [? if unemployed > 15 : However, many male workers develop resentment toward women in the workplace, especially given rising unemployment. ?]

@family
subtitle: Change family and inheritance law to treat women more equally.
on-arrival: family_law += 1; womens_rights += 1; urban_middle_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe -= 2; landless_psoe -= 2; catholic_psoe -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1; ceda_relation -= 4

These reforms establish civil marriage and divorce - both already law under the Republic - on a firmer footing, and extend women's property and inheritance rights within marriage. The more conservative and clerical segments of society treat our reforms as an assault on the family itself.


@welfare
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: welfare += 1; industrial_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); budget -= 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15; unemployed -= 0.4; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.3;

We have increased welfare spending on women and children. [? if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15 : Some of our coalition partners consider increased welfare spending profligate at this time. ?]


@liberalize
max-visits: 1
subtitle: [? if progressive_support < 30 : This is unlikely to succeed; we do not have majority support. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.progressive_support = Q.psoe_r + Q.pce_r + Q.izq_rep_r*0.5;
!}
go-to: liberalize_fail if progressive_support < 30; liberalize_success if progressive_support >= 30

@liberalize_fail
on-arrival: ceda_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1; industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); catholic_psoe -= 5;

Unfortunately, our proposal is voted down in the Cortes, with the CEDA - our long-time adversaries on questions of Church and family - speaking in particularly vehement opposition, and some of our own more Catholic-leaning members breaking party discipline. The activists, feeling demoralized, decide to bide their time.

@liberalize_success
on-arrival: abortion_rights += 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 2; ceda_relation -= 8; catholic_psoe -= 10; radical_relation -= 5; izq_rep_relation += 4; industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); catholic_ceda += 3; catholic_monarchist += 3; industrial_falange -= 3; urban_middle_falange -= 3

With the support of a genuinely progressive bloc - the <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span> and left-leaning republicans - we have successfully passed a bill liberalizing the law on family planning and reproductive rights. This heartens our more progressive supporters, while badly damaging our relations with the CEDA. With the growing political controversy, the CEDA and the monarchist right gain conservative votes at the expense of the Falange, who are seen as having failed to stop it.
